THOUGHT: The NullAway error is because `current` is nullable (see other methods checking `current != null`) but `text()` dereferences it without a check. I should add a null-check in `text()` and keep behavior consistent with `attribute()` and `open()/close()`. After that, I need to run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '478,481s/^  protected void text(@Nullable String text) {
    String existing = current.getText();
    current.setText(existing != null ? existing + text : text);
  }/  protected void text(@Nullable String text) {
    if (current == null) return;
    String existing = current.getText();
    current.setText(existing != null ? existing + text : text);
  }/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/XmlReader.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

